WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.170
- It was Sophia's birthday recently

00:00:01.170 --> 00:00:03.060
and you bought a very
thoughtful gift for her, right?

00:00:03.060 --> 00:00:04.140
- Yeah, I did.

00:00:04.140 --> 00:00:05.806
So I, you know, I wanted to,

00:00:05.806 --> 00:00:09.600
you buy your wife
flowers, the flowers die.

00:00:09.600 --> 00:00:13.770
I wanted to get her flowers
that would last forever.

00:00:13.770 --> 00:00:14.603
- [Kelly] Okay.

00:00:14.603 --> 00:00:15.990
- So, I enlisted the help of this-

00:00:15.990 --> 00:00:16.823
- Harry Potter.

00:00:16.823 --> 00:00:18.240
(laughs)

00:00:18.240 --> 00:00:21.570
- Of this famous glass
sculptor named Martin Blank.

00:00:21.570 --> 00:00:23.850
So, a lot of people know
the name Dale Chihuly

00:00:23.850 --> 00:00:25.918
as far as glass sculpting goes.

00:00:25.918 --> 00:00:29.460
Towards the end of Dale's career,

00:00:29.460 --> 00:00:33.407
Martin was making a lot of
Dale's sculptures for him.

00:00:33.407 --> 00:00:34.650
- Oh, his apprentice basically.

00:00:34.650 --> 00:00:35.528
- Yeah.
- Yeah.

00:00:35.528 --> 00:00:38.130
And there's this brilliant glass
sculptor that's in Seattle.

00:00:38.130 --> 00:00:42.180
And he said, "Hey, I'm gonna
be finishing up the sculpture.

00:00:42.180 --> 00:00:43.590
Do you want to come to Seattle?

00:00:43.590 --> 00:00:46.119
And I'll let you be a part
of it and I'll teach you."

00:00:46.119 --> 00:00:46.952
- [Kelly] Oh, that's you.

00:00:46.952 --> 00:00:48.420
- So, I was taught that that furnace,

00:00:48.420 --> 00:00:50.940
that blast furnace is 2,250 degrees.

00:00:50.940 --> 00:00:53.940
So, you have to be very
careful with everything.

00:00:53.940 --> 00:00:55.440
And there's a dance, there's a movement,

00:00:55.440 --> 00:00:56.490
there's a choreography.

00:00:56.490 --> 00:00:57.323
- Yeah.
- I mean,

00:00:57.323 --> 00:00:58.156
he was basically like,

00:00:58.156 --> 00:01:00.420
"Here are the steps. 1, 2, 3, 4.

00:01:00.420 --> 00:01:01.253
You got it?"

00:01:01.253 --> 00:01:02.317
And it's like,

00:01:02.317 --> 00:01:03.150
- "Okay."
- Yeah.

00:01:03.150 --> 00:01:04.956
- You know, like, don't let anyone die.

00:01:04.956 --> 00:01:05.842
- Don't die.
- Okay. Got it.

00:01:05.842 --> 00:01:06.747
And you don't die, so.

00:01:06.747 --> 00:01:08.370
- So, you did the whole thing?

00:01:08.370 --> 00:01:09.667
- I did, yeah.

00:01:09.667 --> 00:01:12.240
And I made her a surprise,
which I was making there

00:01:12.240 --> 00:01:14.400
which I won't show what
the finish product is,

00:01:14.400 --> 00:01:15.900
- Okay. I like that.
- But that's a surprise.

00:01:15.900 --> 00:01:17.710
- That's so nice though.
That's so beautiful.

00:01:17.710 --> 00:01:19.470
- Yeah.
- It's thoughtful.

00:01:19.470 --> 00:01:21.226
- Yeah and I wanna be a
part of it so that like,

00:01:21.226 --> 00:01:23.940
I could always be a
part of that sculpture.

00:01:23.940 --> 00:01:24.780
- Yeah.
- She knows like,

00:01:24.780 --> 00:01:25.740
know that I made part of it.

00:01:25.740 --> 00:01:27.210
- It's nice too because you can both buy

00:01:27.210 --> 00:01:28.830
whatever you wanna buy,
you know what I'm saying?

00:01:28.830 --> 00:01:31.200
But to make something for
someone, it's beautiful.

00:01:31.200 --> 00:01:32.033
- Sure.

00:01:32.033 --> 00:01:32.866
- Yeah.
- To be a part of it.

00:01:32.866 --> 00:01:34.343
- I think that's more
meaningful. Just saying.

